cyopenworld 1
# The world — six kilometres square, generated from these numbers and from nothing else.
#
# A multi-kilometre world is not committed as data: 2,304 cells of 40 props is 92,160 persistent
# entities, and a repository that carried them would be measuring git rather than the engine. What
# is committed is the DESCRIPTION, and `cy_sample_open-world` cooks the cells from it — deterministic
# in the seed below, so two runs, two machines and two profiles cook the same world.
#
#   extent          cells per side at level 0
#   cell-size       metres per level-0 cell; extent x cell-size is the world's span
#   seed            the only source of variation in the cook
#   props-per-cell  persistent entities per cell
#
# `landmark <x> <z> "<name>" kind <k>` puts one further entity in a named cell. The route passes
# them in order and reports each one by name and kind, which is how a content change becomes
# something the run says out loud.

world "city"
  extent 48
  cell-size 128
  seed 6061
  props-per-cell 40

landmark 4 3   "north-gate"  kind 11
landmark 14 12 "reservoir"   kind 12
landmark 24 22 "relay-mast"  kind 13
landmark 34 32 "foundry"     kind 14
landmark 43 41 "south-yard"  kind 15
